Unicode CLDR spell-out rules (rule-based number format), copied unchanged.

Source:  https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr  tag release-49, folder common/rbnf
         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unicode-org/cldr/release-49/common/rbnf/hi.xml
         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unicode-org/cldr/release-49/common/rbnf/mr.xml
Fetched: 27 Nov 2026
Licence: the header of each file says
         "For terms of use, see http://www.unicode.org/copyright.html"
         "SPDX-License-Identifier: Unicode-DFS-2016"

SHA-256 (shasum -a 256 *.xml):
0e36dbbbf250d7f3faaddc3ff016fc651b1ea8911f9a335c9c296ff7d290a929  hi.xml
78fb9e745590394f35c0a73dc5d78c0f93122df8947b80bf94879a480d580217  mr.xml

Used by tools/gen_numbers.py, which expands the %spellout-cardinal rules for 0 to 999 into
server/lang/numbers_<code>.json. To add a language: download its file from the same folder at the
same tag into this folder, add its hash line above, and run `python tools/gen_numbers.py <code>`.
Do not edit these files or the generated tables by hand.
